Error: Jet.PointOutsideBinding: `point` makes a point, which is declared only as a module binding's value
  --> Tests/UI/point_is_declared_only_as_a_module_binding.jet:3:22
    |
  3 | run: fn() { _: event.point<Int>() }
    |                      ^^^^^
 Why: A point is the module binding it initializes: the program makes its carrier at the first read and every reader shares it, and a call in a body would make a new, anonymous carrier each time it runs
 Fix: Declare it at module level (`clicked: event.point<Int>()`) and use that binding; for a value that is local by design, use `event.new`, `event.hook` or `event.decision_hook`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.PointOutsideBinding
